<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine Tikh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1277</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Constantine Tikh Asen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine Tikh was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1257 to 1277, chosen by the boyars after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-ii-asen">Michael II Asen</a>. A noble of mixed Bulgarian and Serbian descent, he married a granddaughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-asen-ii">Ivan Asen II</a> and later a Byzantine princess to strengthen his claim. His reign saw Mongol raids and Byzantine pressure, and he was killed in 1277 by the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivailo">Ivailo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-tikh.jpg" alt="Constantine Tikh" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bichoes78 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KonstantinTih.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
